description:
A to-do app saves its tasks as JSON. Write:

```csharp
public enum Priority { Low, Normal, High }
public record TodoItem(int Id, string Title, Priority Priority, bool Done, DateOnly? Due);

public static class TodoJson
{
    public static string Save(IEnumerable<TodoItem> items)
    public static List<TodoItem> Load(string json)
    public static List<string> OverdueTitles(string json, DateOnly today)
}
```

- `Save` writes camelCase property names, enums as strings (`"high"` in camelCase too), leaves out `due` when it is null, and is **not** indented.
- `Load` reads what `Save` writes. The JSON text `null`, an empty string or invalid JSON gives an empty list rather than an exception; so do items with a missing or blank title, which are skipped.
- `OverdueTitles` reads the JSON as a tree with `JsonNode` (without deserialising to `TodoItem`) and returns the titles of items that are not done and whose `due` date is before `today`, in file order.

Example of saved JSON: `[{"id":1,"title":"Tea","priority":"high","done":false,"due":"2026-03-01"}]`

